/**
 * Best-known-method efficiency per Slayer task category (community-sourced, not wiki data --
 * see data/slayer-task-weights/SOURCE.txt for provenance and staleness caveats). For each
 * category, this is the single highest raw-profit-per-hour variant/location found in the
 * source spreadsheet's "Mob Data" tab, used to give the player a concrete reason (GP/hr,
 * kills/hr) to judge whether a task is worth doing or worth blocking/skipping.
 *
 * The chosen variant is whatever maximizes profit in the source data, which sometimes means
 * a Wilderness or otherwise risky method (e.g. Callisto for "Bears") -- the variant name is
 * always shown alongside the numbers so the player can judge whether that method is one they
 * actually want to use, rather than presenting the rate as a guaranteed/safe figure.
 *
 * Not every task category has an entry -- the source only tracks tasks worth a block/skip
 * decision, so low-tier tasks (Rats, Cows, Birds, ...) are absent. Callers must handle a
 * null lookup from {@link #EFFICIENCY}.
 */
public final class SlayerTaskEfficiency
{
	public static final class Efficiency
	{
		public final String variant;
		public final double killsPerHour;
		public final double xpPerHour;
		public final double profitPerHour;

